Dear Roger,

I've attached the revised =C2=A72 and =C2=A74 passages with the paragraphs on=
 either side, for our discussion on Wednesday 15 July.

Julie and I read LA-042 as 16 May 1867, rather than 1864. It therefore cannot=
 be the earlier individual loan practice that I had said prepared the January=
 1866 deferment; nor can the March 1866 instruction be described as narrowing=
 that supposedly earlier practice. I've kept the deferment, the March conditi=
ons and the individual permission as separately dated evidence.

Could you look at the two new paragraphs in their surrounding text on the 15t=
h, particularly for any causal connection that I may have left in by implicat=
ion? The change is confined to those arguments and the affected note; it does=
 not alter the January table note.

Many thanks,
Judith


